sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as Platform Gateway / Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS (KServe-managed)
    participant KRP as kube-rbac-proxy sidecar<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS (typical)
    participant MLS as MLServer REST 8080 / gRPC 8081<br/>plaintext, no app auth
    participant RT as Runtime plugin<br/>in-process or parallel worker
    participant SI as KServe storage-initializer
    participant OS as Object storage / PVC / OCI<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Vol as /mnt/models volume
    participant Prom as Prometheus
    participant OTLP as OTLP collector (optional)

    Note over SI,Vol: Flow 2: Model loading at startup
    SI->>OS: Download model artifacts<br/>HTTPS 443, TLS<br/>Storage credentials (platform)
    OS-->>SI: Model artifacts
    SI->>Vol: Write to /mnt/models (filesystem)
    MLS->>Vol: Read */model-settings.json
    MLS->>MLS: Check implementation against<br/>trusted-runtimes.json allowlist (PRODUCTION mode)
    MLS->>RT: Load model (sklearn / xgboost / lightgbm / onnx)

    Note over Client,RT: Flow 1: REST/gRPC inference
    Client->>GW: POST /v2/models/{name}/infer<br/>HTTPS 443, TLS (platform)<br/>Auth: Bearer token
    GW->>KRP: Forward<br/>HTTPS 8443, TLS<br/>Bearer token
    KRP->>KRP: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview
    KRP->>MLS: Forward over localhost<br/>HTTP 8080 or gRPC 8081, no encryption
    MLS->>RT: Dispatch inference (IPC)
    RT-->>MLS: Prediction
    MLS-->>KRP: V2 InferenceResponse
    KRP-->>GW: Response
    GW-->>Client: JSON / protobuf response

    Note over Prom,OTLP: Flow 3: Metrics and tracing
    Prom->>MLS: GET /metrics<br/>HTTP 8082, no TLS, no auth
    MLS-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics
    MLS-)OTLP: Export spans<br/>OTLP/gRPC, insecure=True (hard-coded)
